{"id":1499,"date":"2020-12-01T13:31:31","date_gmt":"2020-12-01T21:31:31","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1499"},"modified":"2024-08-27T12:51:44","modified_gmt":"2024-08-27T19:51:44","slug":"codrone-blockly-jr-flight-directions","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-blockly-jr-flight-directions\/","title":{"rendered":"Flight Directions"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215383a035\" name=\"6a2215383a035\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Flight directions<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Air vehicles move a little differently than land vehicles. While land vehicles can move forward, backward, and<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">sometimes side-to-side, air vehicles can do all of that and move up and down! There are two blocks in the<\/span> fl<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">ight commands menu in Blockly that can help you program your CoDrone to fly in any of these directions.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1500&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215383a163\" name=\"6a2215383a163\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Go for a certain amount of time<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">One of the blocks you can use will make your drone move in the direction you pick for a certain amount of<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">time. All you need to do is drag the go _ for _ seconds block from the flight commands menu to your<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">workspace, pick your direction from the drop-down menu, and then type in the seconds you want your<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CoDrone to travel for. The default power for this block is set to 50%, which means that it will fly at 50% of the<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CoDrone&#8217;s full speed.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1501&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215383a1ca\" name=\"6a2215383a1ca\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Go for a certain amount of time...now with power!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you know how fast (or slow!) you want your CoDrone to go, you can use a different block! Select the go _<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">for _ seconds at _ % power from the flight commands menu, and then use the drop-down menu to pick your<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CoDrone\u2019s direction. Type in your CoDrone\u2019s flight time as well as the power value. This number can range<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">from 0 to 100, with 0 being completely still and 100 being very fast. We recommend starting at 50 and seeing<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">what you need to do from there.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1502&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215383a21c\" name=\"6a2215383a21c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Turn around<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In addition to being able to fly up, down, left, right, forward, and backward, your CoDrone can also turn left<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">and right! There are blocks in the flight commands menu that can help you program your CoDrone to do<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">this:<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1503&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215383a269\" name=\"6a2215383a269\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Turn for a certain amount of time<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To use the turn _ for _ seconds at _ % power block, drag it to your workspace, and then pick left or<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">right from the drop-down menu. Type in the number of seconds you would like your CoDrone to turn for, and<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">then type in the power value. This number can range from 0 to 100, with 0 being completely still and 100<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">being very fast. We recommend starting at 50 and seeing what you need to do from there.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1504&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215383a2b3\" name=\"6a2215383a2b3\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Turn 180 degrees<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you want your CoDrone to turn 180 degrees, there is a block specifically designed for that! Drag the turn<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">180 degrees block to have your CoDrone turn 180 degrees clockwise. <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The default<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">power for this block is set to 50%.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1505&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215383a2f7\" name=\"6a2215383a2f7\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Put it all together!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Try writing a program that will have your CoDrone take off, fly forward, and then turn before landing! It could<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">look something like this:<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1506&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215383a3c9\" name=\"6a2215383a3c9\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<b>Challenge: Shapeshifter<\/b><b>\u00a0<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Have your CoDrone fly in a shape using all of the commands you just learned! The only rule is that you HAVE<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">to include a kill switch.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Some helpful hints:<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A triangle\u2019s angles add up to 180 degrees.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A quadrilateral\u2019s angles add up to 360 degrees.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A pentagon\u2019s angles add up to 540 degrees.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A hexagon\u2019s angles add up to 720 degrees.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">An octagon\u2019s angles add up to 1080 degrees.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 9 Flight directions [vc_column_text]Air vehicles move a little differently than land vehicles. While land vehicles can move forward, backward, and sometimes side-to-side, air vehicles can do all of&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-blockly-jr-flight-directions\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1754,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":806,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1817,1763,1777,1793,626,1533,1438,853,144,167,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2135,2108,2164,2115,2122],"class_list":["post-1499","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-beginner","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-codrone","lesson-tag-flight-directions","lesson-tag-programming","module-junior","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1499","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":6,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1499\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":12715,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1499\/revisions\/12715"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embed